        "path": "_m/g/c/p/v/hackney-empire-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Marie Lloyd Bar, Hackney, E8 (2375176198).jpg",
        "caption": "Attached to the Hackney Empire. Probably the best place to drink in the centre of Hackney (surely preferable to Baxter's Court, the Wetherspoons opposite). Before it was created as part of a 2000 refurbishment of the Empire, there was a pub on the same site. As of 2011, it has closed and been replaced by a cafe.\nAddress: 289 Mare Street.\nFormer Name(s): The Samuel Pepys; The Mr Pepys; The Britannia (all on the same site).\nOwner: Ind Coope (former).\nLinks:\nRandomness Guide to London\n\nDead Pubs (history)",
        "alt": "Attached to the Hackney Empire. Probably the best place to drink in the centre of Hackney (surely preferable to Baxter's Court, the Wetherspoons opposite). Before it was created as part of a 2000 refurbishment of the Empire, there was a pub on the same site. As of 2011, it has closed and been replaced by a cafe.\nAddress: 289 Mare Street.\nFormer Name(s): The Samuel Pepys; The Mr Pepys; The Britannia (all on the same site).\nOwner: Ind Coope (former).\nLinks:\nRandomness Guide to London\n\nDead Pubs (history)",
